# Token saving

- Be concise. Don't restate the request or code back. Summarize; don't paste.
- Start from `memory-bank/` (projectbrief, activeContext, techContext) instead of re-exploring.
- Search first (`rg -n pattern path`), then open only the needed files, and only the relevant line ranges of large files.
- Don't re-read files that haven't changed since you read them.
- Minimal diffs; never rewrite whole files. Batch related edits into one pass.
- Skip generated/vendor dirs (build/, .gradle/, node_modules/, .next/, out/, coverage/).
- Don't print big logs: pipe through `tail -n 40` or `rg -i "error|fail"`.
- No full builds/test suites unless needed; prefer targeted tests (one class/file).
- Ask once only if truly ambiguous; otherwise make a sensible choice and note it.
- After meaningful changes, update `memory-bank/activeContext.md` in 1–3 lines.
